# REQUIRES: verilator
# foldsim-localize-read-addresses: a memory that asks for block RAM, read
# asynchronously at an address whose registers sit in a class kept as an
# instance (Driver/Inputs/localize: the queue's head in class Ptr, the RAM in
# class Leaf). seq-retime-firmem-reads, which inlines only private modules,
# refused it ("address depends on hw.instance"; a32-HX 11-12: the compute
# slice split into execute_slice / issue_slice classes, its ipdom stack's RAM
# read at an address from execute_slice). The class gets an output with the
# next value of the head, the RAM's module a register of it, the read is
# retimed with the boundary kept; virtual (a registered read), it matches the
# target at any latency, with stalls.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/localize
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/lz --static --nest --virtual-memories ram Leaf Ptr > %t/lz.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LOG < %t/lz.log
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RPT < %t/lz/memories.rpt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --top-module tb -DWRITE_FIRST -Mdir %t/lz/obj %S/Inputs/tb_vmem.sv top.sv %t/lz/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/lz/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/lz/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+1 +lo=1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/lz/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+2 +lo=1 +hi=30 +stall=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/lz/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+0 +verilator+seed+3 +lo=5 +hi=60 +full=30 | FileCheck %s
# LOG: foldsim-localize-read-addresses: 1 reads' address registers copied beside their memory
# RPT: Leaf.ram 16x8 ram_style=block converted
# CHECK: {{^}}MATCH
# CHECK-NOT: MISMATCH
